module

public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.SolvableGroupStructure
public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.LinearGroupSchemes

import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.RationalRepresentationComoduleDictionary
import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Flat
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Flat.FaithfullyFlat.Algebra

/-! # Extensions of unitriangular-embeddable affine group schemes

Source: Milne, Algebraic Groups (2017), Section 6.45, printed p.135;
Theorem 14.5(a),(b) and Corollary 14.7, printed pp.281--282
(blueprint: lem-sfb-unitriangular-extension).

A closed embedding into U_n is expressed as a closed group-scheme embedding into GL_n
whose matrices have diagonal entries one and entries below the diagonal zero over every
commutative test algebra. These equations give the same closed subscheme of GL_n as U_n.
No smoothness or reducedness is included in this condition.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- Unitriangular embeddability is preserved by extensions with represented fppf quotient.
The two hypotheses and the conclusion use all algebra-valued points, including nonreduced
algebras, rather than just geometric points. The closed subgroup predicate includes the
homomorphism condition and the closed immersion of underlying schemes.

Source: Milne, Algebraic Groups (2017), Section 6.45, printed p.135;
Theorem 14.5(a),(b) and Corollary 14.7, printed pp.281--282
(blueprint: lem-sfb-unitriangular-extension).

Proof plan, following the six steps of the DAG node:
1. Restrict any nonzero finite-dimensional rational E-representation V to N.
   Apply lem-sfb-unitriangular-subgroup-rational-fixed-vector to obtain a nonzero N-fixed
   vector v over every test algebra. The dictionary
   lem-sfb-rational-representation-comodule-dictionary identifies its coaction with v tensor 1.
2. IsFppfQuotient gives flatness, surjectivity and scheme-theoretic kernel N.
   By lem-weil-pbc-flat-ring-map-iff-flat-affine the coordinate map k[Q] to k[E] is flat;
   lem-weil-pbc-flat-surjective-spectrum-faithfully-flat makes it faithfully flat.
   Apply lem-sfb-central-kernel-cyclic-representation-descent: the E-subcomodule W
   generated by v is nonzero, finite-dimensional and N-trivial, and its action descends to Q.
   Neither centrality nor reducedness of N is needed.
3. Express this descended action as a matrix representation using the dictionary.
   Apply lem-sfb-unitriangular-subgroup-rational-fixed-vector to Q acting on W.
   Its nonzero fixed vector w is E-fixed because the action pulls back along q.
   Its image in V remains nonzero. Thus every nonzero rational E-representation has a
   nonzero fixed vector.
4. Choose a positive-dimensional faithful closed matrix representation of E using
   lem-sfb-affine-group-faithful-linear-representation, valid without smoothness.
5. Induct on the dimension of any representation to construct a complete stable flag
   with trivial successive actions. In dimension zero the flag is empty. Otherwise the
   fixed line kw is trivial; quotient by it and use a linear complement to identify all
   scalar-extended quotients. The quotient action is natural and rational by the dictionary.
   Lift its inductive flag and prepend kw. The induction uses the fixed-vector property
   for the same group E on arbitrary representations, not a quotient-group hypothesis.
6. Choose a basis adapted to the flag of the faithful representation. All matrices over
   every test algebra have entries one on the diagonal and zero below it. In particular
   this holds over k[E] at the universal point, so the coordinate morphism factors through
   the quotient defining U_m. Conjugation preserves the original closed immersion.
   Its surjective coordinate map factors through k[U_m], so the latter map to k[E] is
   surjective too. The affine criterion of def-weil-closed-immersion gives a closed
   immersion into U_m, exactly the asserted unitriangular embedding. -/
theorem unitriangular_embeddable_of_isFppfQuotient
    {k : Type u} [Field k]
    (N E Q : Grp (Over (Spec (.of k))))
    [IsAffine N.X.left] [LocallyOfFiniteType N.X.hom] [QuasiCompact N.X.hom]
    [IsAffine E.X.left] [LocallyOfFiniteType E.X.hom] [QuasiCompact E.X.hom]
    [IsAffine Q.X.left] [LocallyOfFiniteType Q.X.hom] [QuasiCompact Q.X.hom]
    (i : N ⟶ E) (q : E ⟶ Q)
    [IsClosedSubgroupScheme i.hom.hom] [IsNormalSubgroupScheme i.hom.hom]
    (hq : SolvableGroupStructure.IsFppfQuotient i.hom.hom q)
    (hN : ∃ (n : ℕ), 0 < n ∧
      ∃ r : N.X ⟶ GeneralLinearGroup (ULift.{u} (Fin n)) k,
        IsClosedSubgroupScheme r ∧
        ∀ (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [Algebra k A]
          (x : (Spec (.of A)).asOver (Spec (.of k)) ⟶ N.X),
          (∀ a : Fin n,
            (GeneralLinearGroup.homMulEquiv (ULift.{u} (Fin n)) k A (x ≫ r)).val
              ⟨a⟩ ⟨a⟩ = 1) ∧
          (∀ a b : Fin n, b < a →
            (GeneralLinearGroup.homMulEquiv (ULift.{u} (Fin n)) k A (x ≫ r)).val
              ⟨a⟩ ⟨b⟩ = 0))
    (hQ : ∃ (n : ℕ), 0 < n ∧
      ∃ r : Q.X ⟶ GeneralLinearGroup (ULift.{u} (Fin n)) k,
        IsClosedSubgroupScheme r ∧
        ∀ (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [Algebra k A]
          (x : (Spec (.of A)).asOver (Spec (.of k)) ⟶ Q.X),
          (∀ a : Fin n,
            (GeneralLinearGroup.homMulEquiv (ULift.{u} (Fin n)) k A (x ≫ r)).val
              ⟨a⟩ ⟨a⟩ = 1) ∧
          (∀ a b : Fin n, b < a →
            (GeneralLinearGroup.homMulEquiv (ULift.{u} (Fin n)) k A (x ≫ r)).val
              ⟨a⟩ ⟨b⟩ = 0)) :
    ∃ (n : ℕ), 0 < n ∧
      ∃ r : E.X ⟶ GeneralLinearGroup (ULift.{u} (Fin n)) k,
        IsClosedSubgroupScheme r ∧
        ∀ (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [Algebra k A]
          (x : (Spec (.of A)).asOver (Spec (.of k)) ⟶ E.X),
          (∀ a : Fin n,
            (GeneralLinearGroup.homMulEquiv (ULift.{u} (Fin n)) k A (x ≫ r)).val
              ⟨a⟩ ⟨a⟩ = 1) ∧
          (∀ a b : Fin n, b < a →
            (GeneralLinearGroup.homMulEquiv (ULift.{u} (Fin n)) k A (x ≫ r)).val
              ⟨a⟩ ⟨b⟩ = 0) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
